P1 — non-agent completion filter
================================
origin:   BryanChen408/ProRL-Agent-Server (fork), commits d764ecce0d0b
          ("Filter non-trainable completions in trajectory builders",
          2026-06-21) + cb6132824ad4 (shape-only fix: drop the content
          whitelist, 2026-07-27), squashed to the post-fix state and
          hand-adapted to upstream stable @ f0e8343a (fork base = stable~2;
          neither commit cherry-picks cleanly).
what:     Adds src/polar/trajectory/builder/record_filters.py — a shape-only
          _is_non_agent_side_completion (single user message, no system, no
          tools, no SDK-only keys => non-agent) plus truncated-marker and
          empty-choices filters — and wires filter_trainable_completions()
          into both builders (per_request, prefix_merging). All-filtered
          sessions => trajectory ERROR "no trainable completions after
          completion filter"; filter bookkeeping lands in trajectory
          metadata under "completion_filter"; prefix_merging stats gain
          raw_completions_total (pre-filter) next to completions_total
          (post-filter).
why:      CP-02/D1, confirmed WORSE than reported: upstream at the pin has
          NO non-agent filter at all (record_filters.py is fork-born), so
          every auxiliary harness LLM call becomes a well-formed
          chain_length=1 trainable trace carrying full session reward.
          Fork validation: 38/38 dirty caught, 0/1488 false kills, measured
          density up to 27% of a batch. This patch is ADDITIVE at the pin,
          not a fix of existing upstream code.
evidence: docs/reports/CP-02.md defect table D1; ADR-0004.
!! FLAG:  The shape criteria were validated against a DIFFERENT harness's
!!        wire dialect (Anthropic-API-shaped: top-level `system` key,
!!        `thinking` / `stream` / `context_management` / `output_config`).
!!        They MUST be re-validated against pi 0.83.0's actual wire dialect
!!        at CP-06 (charter A-12) before any gsj rollout is trusted.
adaptation vs fork:
          - squashed to the post-fix filter (the content whitelist never
            existed in this repo's history);
          - prefix_merging hunks re-authored against pin context (pin's
            stats dict has no completions_preserved/completions_dropped;
            pin metadata uses len(chains), not len(final_traces));
          - fork's builder-level tests re-hosted in the new
            tests/trajectory/test_builder_filter_wiring.py (the fork-base
            test files don't match / don't exist at the pin);
          - four pin fixture sites amended with the fork's own
            "system": "harness" agent-side marker (two tests in
            test_per_request_builder.py + two shared record helpers in
            test_engine_trajectory_equivalence.py feeding six tests — their
            bare single-user-message requests are exactly the shape the
            filter drops);
          - tests/trajectory/test_record_filters.py is fork-verbatim.

